From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Fri, 09 Oct 2026 10:03:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: keep the AP width after a background chain search

When no channel fits a background chain at the AP width, the search
narrows the width in the AP configuration and does not restore it.
The radio keeps its real width, but later beacon updates, channel
switches and restarts use the narrower width.

The AP configuration now keeps its width after the search. Only the
CAC on the background chain uses the narrower width that the search
selected. A radar on the operating channel can still narrow the AP,
because the AP then moves to the selected channel at that width. A
failed search also clears the CAC flag of the record, because a set
flag stops a later channel switch from arming a new chain.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 src/ap/dfs.c |    6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/dfs.c
+++ b/src/ap/dfs.c
@@ -1133,6 +1133,9 @@ static void hostapd_dfs_update_backgroun
 	struct hostapd_channel_data *channel;
 	u8 oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx = 0;
 	u8 oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx = 0;
+	/* the search narrows the AP config; the AP keeps its own width */
+	enum oper_chan_width oper_chwidth =
+		hostapd_get_oper_chwidth(iface->conf);
 
 	/*
 	 * Allow selection of DFS channel in ETSI to comply with
@@ -1161,10 +1164,13 @@ static void hostapd_dfs_update_backgroun
 				  sec, hostapd_get_oper_chwidth(iface->conf),
 				  oper_centr_freq_seg0_idx,
 				  oper_centr_freq_seg1_idx, true)) {
+		hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf, oper_chwidth);
 		wpa_printf(MSG_ERROR, "DFS failed to start CAC offchannel");
 		iface->radar_background.channel = -1;
+		iface->radar_background.cac_started = 0;
 		return;
 	}
+	hostapd_set_oper_chwidth(iface->conf, oper_chwidth);
 
 	iface->radar_background.channel = channel->chan;
 	iface->radar_background.freq = channel->freq;
